    "final_text": "I fixed ISSUE-214: `buildUrl` now keeps `retry=0` and `include_archived=false`. The full test suite passes (10 of 10, run through `dx run-gate --name full-gate`).\n\n**Cause:** the query serializer in `src/url-builder.js` skipped every falsy value, not just missing ones.\n- `serializeQuery` (line 126) had `if (!value) continue;`\n- `appendQueryValue` (line 137) had `if (!item) continue;` for array items\n\nSo `0` and `false` were dropped along with `null` and `undefined`. That's also why the reporter's workaround of passing strings worked: `'0'` counts as true in JavaScript.\n\n**Fix:** a two-line change. Both checks now skip only `null` and `undefined`, the same rule `normalizePath` already uses for path segments at line 74. `buildSignedUrl` goes through the same code, so it's fixed too. The API is unchanged and nothing else was touched.\n\n**Regression tests** (in `tests/url-builder.test.js`):\n- `buildUrl keeps retry=0 and include_archived=false query values (ISSUE-214)`: the exact case from the issue.\n- `serializeQuery keeps 0 and false inside array values`: arrays had the same bug.\n- `serializeQuery omits only null and undefined values`: `null` and `undefined` are still left out.\n\nAll three failed on the original code, showing the dropped keys, and pass with the fix.\n\n**One behavior change to know about:** an empty string is now sent as `key=` instead of being dropped. I did this on purpose: it's a value the caller passed, and the browser's standard `URLSearchParams` handles it the same way. But a caller that relied on `''` being omitted, such as `cursor: ''` for a first page, would now send `cursor=`. If you'd rather keep dropping empty strings, add `|| value === ''` to the two checks. The `Resolution` section in `ISSUE.md` explains the cause, the fix, the tests, and this change.\n\nThe changes are uncommitted in the working tree on `main`.",
